# promise: #744
# An extension's ⌘ shortcut typed while a page has the keyboard opens its popup, as in Chrome and Arc, where an
# extension's shortcuts come before the page. Cra hands ⌘ keys to the page first (CraApplication.sendEvent, Chrome's
# rule for pages), past the app-wide watch that runs extensions' shortcuts, and what the page left went to Cra's own
# commands only: Obsidian Web Clipper's ⌘⇧O, or any ⌘ key set for "Activate the extension", did nothing, while its
# ⌥⇧ shortcuts worked. The keys go to the page's view as a typed ⌘ key does, with the toolbar hidden (Arc's default):
# ⌘⇧Y, which Cra has no command for, and ⌘⇧O, Cra's dimmed Show Little Window "Open In" Menu in a browser window.
budget rss=900 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/PageShortcutExtension
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/ShortcutOverCraExtension
relaunch
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=page-shortcut
wait 3
cra://debug?chromePref=extensions.commands
expect-log chrome pref extensions\.commands: .*"mac:Command\+Shift\+Y":\{"command_name":"_execute_action"
cra://debug?key=Y,16,1179648&page=1&source=keyboard
expect-log extension command [a-p]{8}: opens its popup
expect-log "GET /page\.html\?n=page-shortcut-popup-opened HTTP
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://debug?key=O,31,1179648&page=1&source=keyboard
expect-log "GET /page\.html\?n=shortcut-over-cra-popup-opened HTTP
